12
00:39:05,806 --> 00:39:11,806
Oklahoma City (  OH-klə-HOH-mə -⁠), often shortened to OKC, is
the capital and most populous city of the U.S.

13
00:42:21,290 --> 00:42:27,290
state of Oklahoma.

14
00:45:36,774 --> 00:45:42,774
It is the 20th-most populous U.S.

15
00:48:52,258 --> 00:48:58,258
city and 8th largest in the Southern United States, with a
population of 681,054 at the 2020 census.

16
00:52:07,741 --> 00:52:13,741
The Oklahoma City metropolitan area, with an estimated 1.49 million residents, is the
largest metropolitan area in the state and 42nd-most populous in the country.

17
00:55:23,225 --> 00:55:29,225
It is the county seat of Oklahoma County, with the city limits extending into Canadian, Cleveland, and Pottawatomie counties; however,
areas beyond Oklahoma County primarily consist of suburban developments or areas designated rural and watershed zones.

18
00:58:38,709 --> 00:58:44,709
Oklahoma City ranks as the tenth-largest city by area in the United States when including
consolidated city-counties, and second-largest when such consolidations are excluded.

19
01:01:54,193 --> 01:02:00,193
It is also the second-largest state capital by area, after Juneau, Alaska.

20
01:05:09,677 --> 01:05:15,677
Oklahoma City has one of the world's largest livestock markets.

21
01:08:25,161 --> 01:08:31,161
Oil, natural gas, petroleum products, and related
industries are its economy's largest sector.

22
01:11:40,645 --> 01:11:46,645
The city is in the middle of an active oil field, and
oil derricks dot the capitol grounds.

23
01:14:56,129 --> 01:15:02,129
The federal government employs a large number of workers at Tinker Air Force Base and the United States Department of Transportation's Mike Monroney Aeronautical
Center (which house offices of the Federal Aviation Administration and the Transportation Department's Enterprise Service Center, respectively).

24
01:18:11,612 --> 01:18:17,612
Oklahoma City is on the I-35 and I-40 corridors, one of the primary travel corridors south into Texas and New Mexico,
north towards Wichita and Kansas City, west towards Albuquerque, and east towards Little Rock and Memphis.

25
01:21:27,096 --> 01:21:33,096
Located in the state's Frontier Country region, the city's northeast
section lies in an ecological region known as the Cross Timbers.

26
01:24:42,580 --> 01:24:48,580
The city was founded during the Land Run of 1889 and grew to a
population of over 10,000 within hours of its founding.

27
01:27:58,064 --> 01:28:04,064
It was the site of the April 19, 1995 bombing of the Alfred P.

28
01:31:13,548 --> 01:31:19,548
Murrah Federal Building, in which 168 people died.

29
01:34:29,032 --> 01:34:35,032
Since weather records have been kept beginning in 1890, Oklahoma City has been struck by 13 violent tornadoes, 11 of
which were rated F4 or EF4 on the Fujita and Enhanced Fujita scales, and two which were rated F5 or EF5.

30
01:37:44,516 --> 01:37:50,516
The film explores themes of oklahoma city bombing,
terrorism, bombing, aryanism, american experience.
